      "text": "We first identify the terms in the sequence. The sequence is given by the sum of consecutive powers of 3. Thus, the first term is:\n\n\\[\n3^0\n\\]\n\nThe second term is:\n\n\\[\n3^0 + 3^1\n\\]\n\nThe third term is:\n\n\\[\n3^0 + 3^1 + 3^2\n\\]\n\nAnd the fourth term is:\n\n\\[\n3^0 + 3^1 + 3^2 + 3^3\n\\]\n\nTo find the simplified value of the fourth term, we sum the following sequence of powers of 3:\n\n\\[\n3^0 + 3^1 + 3^2 + 3^3\n\\]\n\nRecall that:\n\n\\[\n3^0 = 1\n\\]\n\n\\[\n3^1 = 3\n\\]\n\n\\[\n3^2 = 9\n\\]\n\n\\[\n3^3 = 27\n\\]\n\nNow, we sum these values:\n\n\\[\n1 + 3 + 9 + 27\n\\]\n\nLet's perform the addition step-by-step:\n\n\\[\n1 + 3 = 4\n\\]\n\n\\[\n4 + 9 = 13\n\\]\n\n\\[\n13 + 27 = 40\n\\]\n\nThus, the simplified value of the fourth term in the sequence is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{40}\n\\]",
