      "text": "The sequence given is a sum of consecutive powers of 3, starting from $3^0$. Each term in the sequence is formed by adding the current power of 3 to the previous terms. We are asked to find the simplified value of the fourth term of this sequence.\n\nLet's denote the $n$-th term of the sequence by $a_n$. The sequence starts as follows:\n\n\\[\na_0 = 3^0 = 1\n\\]\n\nThe second term is:\n\n\\[\na_1 = 3^0 + 3^1 = 1 + 3 = 4\n\\]\n\nThe third term is:\n\n\\[\na_2 = 3^0 + 3^1 + 3^2 = 1 + 3 + 9 = 13\n\\]\n\nThe fourth term is:\n\n\\[\na_3 = 3^0 + 3^1 + 3^2 + 3^3 = 1 + 3 + 9 + 27 = 40\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the simplified value of the fourth term of the sequence is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{40}\n\\]",
